  },
  "articleBody": "Embarking on a tiny home journey is exciting, but there are a few common pitfalls we see folks stumble into during the planning phase. Avoiding these can save you headaches and help you achieve your dream tiny living experience. One major mistake is not assessing your property's specific conditions early enough. Things like topography, access to utilities, and even local zoning laws can drastically impact your design and placement options. We always recommend a thorough property assessment right from the start to avoid unexpected roadblocks. Another common error is failing to truly define your lifestyle needs before designing. If you love to cook, you'll need a different kitchen layout than someone who eats out every night. Don't just pick a pretty floor plan; make sure it supports how you genuinely live. Also, many underestimate the importance of smart, integrated storage. Without it, even the most beautiful tiny home becomes a mess. Think about built-ins, vertical solutions, and multi-functional pieces from day one. Lastly, trying to fit too much into a small footprint is a classic mistake. Sometimes, less really is more. Focus on quality over quantity and allow for open space to avoid feeling cramped. Getting professional guidance early can help you navigate these complexities and ensure your tiny home is truly functional and comfortable.",
